+`check` rebuilds production output and runs source/VM regressions, real image
+full-decode checks, and PostgreSQL migrations/RPC/RLS tests using PGlite.
+`verify:browser` writes the responsive public/login matrix under
+`artifacts/browser-verification`. It uses a local verification configuration;
+run `npm run build` with the intended environment after it finishes.
+`verify:editor` builds and exercises the real UI against the isolated loopback
+fixture, including concurrent saves, failure recovery, selection, gallery
+upload, publication, restore, sign-out, and Viewer restrictions. Its evidence
+is under `artifacts/editor-verification`.
+
+Install Chrome/Chromium and set `CHROME_PATH` for both browser commands. Set
+`CHROME_NO_SANDBOX=true` only in a disposable container that cannot run Chrome's
+sandbox. The browser fixture never connects to Supabase. PGlite executes real
+PostgreSQL with minimal Auth/Storage schema shims; real GoTrue, Storage HTTP,
+Realtime, hosted routing, and deployed Edge behavior still require staging.
+No live Supabase mutations were performed.
+
+There is no separate lint command. `typecheck:edge` checks the Edge TypeScript
+against the installed, pinned npm packages. JSX compilation is checked by the
+build; a whole-frontend type-check is not configured.
+
+See `docs/FINAL_VERIFICATION_REPORT.md` for the audited baseline, confirmed
+issues, changed-file inventory, evidence, and GitHub update instructions.
 
